                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237392881",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199057365788",
                            "num_reviews": 18,
                            "playtime_forever": 345,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 345,
                            "last_played": 1791636392
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Whereas Narcissu 1st & 2nd explore the acceptance of death as an inevitability and the desperate yearning to live in the face of cruel fate, Ame no Marginal is a journey of confronting a much more existential question: What does it mean to live in this world? The game retains the distinctive artistic style of Narcissu, alongside Kataoka Tomo’s exceptional writing, which masterfully lays bare the characters’ emotions and innermost thoughts.\r\nHighly recommended for reading on rainy days and nights. Seriously, the rain makes the experience so much better. Nothing quite complements an existential crisis like staring out the window while it pours outside. Just make sure the weather is suitably gloomy, the room is quiet, and your life is at least somewhat stable before you start playing.\r\nBecause apparently, the best way to spend a rainy night is to question the meaning of existence with a visual novel. And if it starts raining while you’re playing, congratulations! You’ve unlocked the premium atmospheric experience at absolutely no extra cost.\r\n",
